{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.619 accuracy, far exceeding image_only config_003 (0.328), confirming RNA is critical. The image modality alone contributed ~0.33, suggesting the image encoder has room to improve. Question: config_015 is a clean single-variable ablation of config_009, swapping resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical (pca_n2000, avgpool, concat, multiprofile). This isolates whether a stronger image backbone (ViT-L vs ResNet50) yields meaningful accuracy gains. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether the image encoder is a bottleneck is high-value; if ViT-L helps, subsequent experiments can combine it with better RNA encoders (scgpt/scvi_n200) and transformer aggregation. If it does not, we can focus budget on RNA-side improvements. Expected cost: ViT-L is a larger backbone than ResNet50, so I estimate ~45–55 GPU hours (roughly 1.3–1.5× config_009's 36.42 h), which is acceptable given the potential accuracy gain and the remaining budget."
}

